7. NORMALIZATION DESIGN
============================================================

Account normalization must:

- convert numeric Excel account values to stable strings;
- remove artificial `.0`;
- protect leading zeros where configured;
- trim whitespace;
- preserve the original account value;
- reject malformed values through a controlled warning.

Amount normalization must:

- remove commas and spaces;
- support parentheses as negatives;
- support explicit negative signs;
- handle blank and null cells;
- distinguish zero from missing;
- parse through Decimal;
- preserve the original text;
- never silently convert invalid text to zero.

Description normalization must:

- trim spaces;
- normalize repeated whitespace;
- normalize common punctuation variants;
- create an uppercase matching form;
- retain the original description;
- preserve meaningful accounting terms.

Row classification must identify:

- POSTING;
- PARENT;
- SUBTOTAL;
- TOTAL;
- GRAND_TOTAL;
- HEADER;
- BLANK;
- TEMPLATE;
- UNKNOWN.

Parent and control rows must not be added to their detailed child balances unless explicitly marked as independently posting.


