A. Central Bank calculator

Formula:

A-CBI
+ A-CRR
+ other approved Central Bank components
= Balances with Central Bank

Illustrative Iraq account calculation:

183110
+ 183120
+ eligible 183130
= Balances with Central Bank

Include Schedule 3 reconciliation.

B. Bank balances calculator

Calculate asset and liability sides separately.

Asset side:

A-IGA
+ A-IBA
= Debit Balances with Banks

Liability side:

L-IGL-C
+ L-IGL-F
+ L-IBL
= Bank and Group Liabilities

Do not automatically offset liability balances against asset balances.

Where a schedule contains a net informational balance, calculate it separately and label it as schedule information.

C. Investment calculator

Formula may include:

principal
+ premium
- discount
+ approved positive MTM
- approved negative MTM
- impairment
± approved carrying-value adjustment

Do not automatically include an equity reserve in the asset carrying amount unless the approved mapping specifically instructs this treatment.

D. Fixed asset calculator

Formula:

fixed asset costs
+ eligible WIP
± approved fixed asset clearing
- accumulated depreciation
- asset impairment
= Net Fixed Assets

The calculator must expose each component separately.

E. Other asset calculator

Aggregate only approved A-OA accounts.

Do not use Other Assets as an automatic residual plug.

F. Capital and reserves calculator

Calculate categories separately before producing any financial statement subtotal.

G. Customer deposits calculator

Retain product classifications such as:

- current;
- savings;
- term;
- customer;
- bank;
- group;
- other deposit.

H. Provisions calculator

Distinguish:

- tax;
- employee;
- bonus;
- holiday;
- gratuity;
- ECL;
- investment impairment;
- other provisions.

Do not treat every provision as an ordinary liability.

I. Spot-position calculator

Process SPOT separately.

Do not absorb SPOT into Other Assets or Other Liabilities unless an approved final presentation rule explicitly requires it.

J. Off-balance-sheet calculator

Process:

- OBS-Gtee;
- OBS-Contra;
- guarantees;
- letters of credit;
- FX forwards;
- contingent accounts;
- memorandum accounts.

Exclude all approved OFF BS balances from primary balance-sheet totals.


