============================================================
14. CONTROLLED COMBINATION MATCHING
============================================================

Combination matching is an exception-analysis function, not a primary mapping method.

Only run it for unresolved financial statement lines or unmapped accounts.

Required constraints:

- configurable maximum combination size;
- same statement type;
- compatible natural side;
- same unit basis;
- compatible currency basis;
- semantic compatibility;
- no parent rows;
- no control totals;
- no previously consumed account unless split allocation is allowed;
- no mixing of BS and OFF BS;
- no mixing of P&L and BS;
- no asset-liability netting without a presentation rule.

Prefer:

- the smallest coherent account set;
- approved semantic proximity;
- lower complexity;
- exact or near-exact amount.

Classify numerical-only matches as provisional.

Do not automatically approve them.


