============================================================
16. VARIANCE AND TOLERANCE ENGINE
============================================================

For every line calculate:

Calculated Amount
= sum of presented account contributions

Variance
= Calculated Amount - Reported Amount

Absolute Variance
= absolute value of Variance

Variance Percentage
= Absolute Variance / absolute value of Reported Amount

Where the reported amount is zero, return variance percentage as not applicable.

Use configurable tolerances.

Suggested status hierarchy:

- EXACT_MATCH;
- PRECISION_MATCH;
- ROUNDING_MATCH;
- PARTIAL_MATCH;
- MATERIAL_BREAK;
- MAPPING_DIFFERENCE;
- PRESENTATION_DIFFERENCE;
- UNIT_DIFFERENCE;
- SIGN_DIFFERENCE;
- SCHEDULE_DIFFERENCE;
- SOURCE_DATA_DIFFERENCE;
- UNMAPPED_ACCOUNT;
- DUPLICATE_MAPPING;
- OFF_BS_EXCLUSION;
- UNRESOLVED.

Do not replace the actual variance with zero after applying tolerance.


